# Codex Session Bootstrap

Read `AGENTS.md` completely first, then follow its required reading order.

For full-game or bridge work, also read:

- `docs/PHASE_1_ASTRA_HANDOFF.md` for the active 23cf checkout; local main is older
- `docs/PHASE_1_GENERIC_EVENT_HANDLER_PLAN.md` for the clarified event priority
- `docs/PHASE_1_CURRENT_STATUS.md`
- `docs/PHASE_1_ACTOR_READY_EXECUTION_PLAN.md`
- `docs/research/PHASE_1_ACTOR_READY_ACCEPTANCE.md`
- `docs/MULTI_AGENT_EXECUTION.md`
- `docs/PHASE_1_NEXT_INCREMENT_PLAN.md` and its acceptance ledger for the
  completed predecessor contracts
- `bridge/Sts2AgentBridge/README.md`

For headless actor packets, inspect the accepted boundaries in:

- `game/contracts/headless_v0.py`
- `game/backends/headless/reduced_run_backend.py`
- `game/data/headless_trajectory.py`
- `game/training/headless_reporting.py`
- `game/training/headless_rollout.py` when collection changes

Most important code after that:

- `game/simulation/core.py`
- `game/simulation/encoding.py`
- `game/cli/train.py`

The live integration milestone remains `R0i`. Generic event v6 is the latest
accepted functional component: singleton potion/relic children plus retained
upgrade/removal/reward/transform families and separate cumulative completion.
Read its contract and acceptance ledger via the Astra handoff. All 26 successors
are frozen. Remaining families include multiple-offer items, optional/scrolling
selectors, variable minima and custom/combat interactions. All live campaigns
are closed; no game setup is needed before a new reviewed release is ready.
An installable G6 release, live item/transform support and a complete autonomous
run remain unclaimed.

Key invariants:

- keep structured observations separate from RL encoding
- keep stable enemy slots in multi-enemy combat
- keep action masks aligned with action encoding
- keep reward shaping oriented toward winning with more HP left
- maintain Python `3.10+` compatibility
